  "script": "Apple's iPhone 18 Pro has a new signature color.\n\nIt's called Dark Cherry — and nobody agrees what it looks like.\n\nWhich is odd, because we know its exact Pantone code.\n\nAnd here's the catch: Apple's most expensive iPhone ever doesn't get it.\n\nBut first — what color is this actually?\n\nEvery render you've seen leans red.\n\nBut the leaker who detailed it says those are wrong. It's purple-tinged.\n\nAnd the reports pin it to one number: Pantone 6076.\n\nPantone files that under Red-Purple. In plain terms: a dark plum.\n\nSo if you're picturing a rich red iPhone, the real one is quieter and browner than you expect.\n\nIt's still the only risk in the lineup: Silver, Dark Gray, and a Light Blue.\n\nAnd reports don't even agree Dark Gray survives.\n\nNow — that most expensive iPhone.\n\nThe foldable iPhone Ultra reportedly gets two. Silver, and a dark blue.\n\nBoth from leaked camera protectors, not the phone.\n\nA bold color is a bet. Sell millions and a miss gets absorbed — but at a reported two thousand dollars and up, it's just unsold stock.\n\nSo the risk goes where the volume is.\n\nNone of it's confirmed — and lighting changes how any color reads.\n\nSo — plum, not red. Still the one you'd pick?",
